= Metadata — Simple =

'''Metadata''' is structured information that describes a resource.

Examples for a photo:

* who took it;
* when it was taken;
* camera model;
* location;
* file format.

Examples for a book:

* title;
* author;
* subject;
* publication date;
* ISBN.

Metadata helps people and computers find, manage and understand resources.

The phrase "data about data" is useful, but metadata can describe much more than data. It can describe people, physical objects, services, or concepts.

Metadata can also record [[Provenance/Simple|provenance]]: where something came from and how it changed.

